  "body": "## What changed\n\nOne rule for every stock or verdict lattice sized from a length: a side within a relative 1e-9 of a whole number of cells gets that whole number of cells; a real part of a cell still gets its cell.\n\n- `stock_sim::kernel::cells_across(extent, cell)` counts cells across a length.\n- `stock_sim::kernel::edge_cells(v, cell, upper)` (new) is the same law for an edge locked to the origin.\n\nSites on the rule:\n- `Dexel::block` (column stock).\n- The field box gate and the field cylinder gate (`backend_build.rs`). The cylinder gate counts the circumscribed square the column arm builds.\n- The exact carry read `History::read` (`carry_exact.rs`), with `.max(1)`, so a thin box keeps one column.\n- The field arm's verdict lattice `lattice_of` (`march.rs`), by `edge_cells`.\n- The side-on slabs of a cut body (`carry_side.rs`), with `.max(1)`.\n- The mesh stock gate on both arms, `from_facets` (`cut.rs`, `backend_build.rs`), plus the one cell of margin each side.\n\nLeft as they are, because they hold no stock and the case cannot arise there: the edge-break window in `wall_anchor.rs` divides by 256 (exact), and the `scan.rs` envelope grid has a full margin of air beyond the part.\n\n## Readings\n\nA 12.7 mm side two ulps long over a 0.254 mm cell:\n- Block and exact carry: 50 columns (was 51). No material past the box edge (was up to one cell).\n- Field verdict lattice: 50 columns (was 51, against the column arm's 50).\n- Side-on carry of a cut body: 50 slabs (was 51).\n- Mesh stock on either arm: 52 columns with the margin (was 53). A strip 4094 cells a few ulps long now builds on both arms (was refused as 4097).\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n`crates/sim/src/stock_sim/cell_count_tests.rs`, synthetic shapes only, 9 tests:\n- `a_whole_number_of_cells_up_to_rounding_is_that_number`\n- `no_material_stands_past_a_box_edge_read_a_few_ulps_long`\n- `the_cell_ceiling_gate_counts_the_same_columns`\n- `the_exact_carry_read_counts_the_blocks_columns`\n- `the_field_box_gate_counts_the_same_columns`\n- `both_cylinder_gates_count_the_same_columns`\n- `the_field_verdict_lattice_over_a_box_has_the_column_arms_columns`\n- `the_side_on_carry_slices_a_height_a_few_ulps_over_whole_cells_into_whole_slabs`\n- `both_mesh_stock_gates_count_the_same_columns`\n\nEach site set back to its old count turns its test red; with the rule, all 9 pass.\n\n## Gates\n\nOn the final head c2dcb516c (upstream/main merged in):\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 83 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (29.6 min).\n- `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cell_count_tests`: 9 passed, 0 failed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The heavy lanes and the light gate (release build of the app).\n- The GUI.\n\n## Related\n\n- #4047: a cylinder stock over about 1000 cells across builds on the column arm and is refused on the field arm by the per-facet cell budget in `field_gen.rs`. Measured on main; not changed here.\n\nEffort: high (stock simulation is under the safety floor).\nChangelog: Stock: a side a few ulps longer than a whole number of cells no longer gets an extra column, slab or verdict cell, on either backend.\n\nBranch: upstream/main merged in (plain merge); the diff is 9 files: the 7 source files above, the test file, and the one `mod.rs` line that registers it.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #4012\n",
